<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21234] Lustre delayed work runs on isolated CPUs and stalls DNE lock cancels</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21234</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;On servers whose isolcpus cores are held by SCHED_FIFO tasks, DNE lock cancels can hang for many minutes after a large unlink:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;Lustre: ldlm_cn00_007: service thread pid 37083 was inactive for 3660.157 seconds.
 __flush_work+0x26b/0x380
 tgt_sync+0x127/0x150 [ptlrpc]
 tgt_blocking_ast+0x2ac/0x750 [ptlrpc]
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Delayed work queued without naming a CPU runs on whichever CPU its timer expires on. On Linux 6.9 to 6.18 that can be an isolated CPU, where the work gets only a few percent of the CPU (fixed in 6.19 by 7dec062cfcf2, not in RHEL 10). tgt_sync() waits for the lu_site_flush pass, so ldlm_cn threads wait too. On master, the PM QoS work, ldlm pool recalc and service watchdog also run on isolated CPUs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reproduced on a single-node DNE VM with isolcpus=2,3 and busy loops on those CPUs: during an rm -rf of 60000 files, a flush pass took 140s and a cross-MDT mkdir 23s.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fix: queue delayed work that does not name a CPU on unbound workqueues, which stay off isolated CPUs. With that, the same test ran no Lustre work on the isolated CPUs, and nothing took over 2s.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
